  "worked_solution": "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+{y}^{2}}{x} & =c \\\\ x+{y}^{2} & =cx \\\\ x(1-c)+{y}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1,$ the level curve is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2},$ which is a parabola that opens to the left (excluding the origin). So, I is false.\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curves is $x=-{y}^{2},$ which is a parabola that opens to the left (excluding the origin). So, II is true.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is $y=0,$ which is the $x$-axis (excluding the origin). So, III is true.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
